        <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides strongly-typed constants corresponding to the <computeroutput>MPTAR_TYPE_*</computeroutput> macro definitions. Regular files can be encoded as either <ref refid="group__mptar__typeflags_1ga69a24759c7606a35f42b2e9eb7fbf9d6" kindref="member">MPTAR_TYPE_FILE</ref> (&apos;0&apos;) or <ref refid="group__mptar__typeflags_1gabbc1ace27b004e4af7e9f05b91eceef7" kindref="member">MPTAR_TYPE_FILE_LEGACY</ref> (&apos;\0&apos;); parsers should check for both types when identifying standard files. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
